{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms","id":547222,"title":"Why not obvious Atavisms?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-09T10:02:23-07:00","id":547222,"title":"Why not obvious Atavisms?","content":"As I preper to include the mythical horror of <b>Beast </b>in to mine games, I have one question - <b>Why Atavisms are not visible to <i>anyone</i>?</b> The are to be seen only to at least minor supernatural templates. I do not get idea beside this concept - can someone from <b>Beast</b>'s developers team answer to me on this?<br /> <br /> It's wierd, as the Children in RAW do not need to conceal they existance to humanity - contrary to<a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/Masquerade\" target=\"_blank\">Masquerade</a>, &quot;The Herd Must Not Know&quot; or Percept of Secrecy, too mention only the Big Three of WoD settings. It's even stranger when you concider that Beasts want to be other supernaturals family - so they would want to play by the others rules, i.e. not using their powers ostensibly on humans, or their vampires, werewolves or changeling cousins <i>will </i>talk about it with them. And taking in account the effects of powers are visible - dragon's fire <b>is</b> burining ground, Raptor's claws <b>are</b> slashing objects, Makra's tentacles <b>are</b> suffocating people in the room - why some physical, obvious changes are not shown in Atavisms of Begotten?<br /> <br /> Like the Ugallu's hands become real birds claws for those few second. Or Beast with Dragon's Soul just spits fire from scaled head on his victims for one turn. Why Soul cannot be shown in slight why to everyone watching, and is visible only to those with supernatural powers?<br /> <br /> It's seems very illogical and counter-intuitive in setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-09-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:20:25-07:00","id":547262,"title":"","content":"Well, one thing is that the whole masquerade system is generally reinforced by magic, not laws. As the WoD games went on and on, you'll notice there's less and less &quot;laws&quot; over the matter, and more supernatural consequences. Vampires have the mind-bluring Kiss and the mirror effects. Werewolves have Lunacy. Mages avoid it because of 'dox. Prommies to disquiet, changelings to attracting the Others, Mummies to do their cult-brainwashing thing, GtSE to not annoy their geister. In Demon, its to avoid Compromise. <br /> <br /> Secrecy is literally part of their nature. So, tied into that, invisible Atavism might be part of it. You can't go walking down Main Street looking like a dragon. Werewolves cover their shapeshifting with Lunacy. Demons with compromises. And so on. Obvious shapeshifting has its own secrecy laws - in this case, its &quot;no one sees it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another part of it might be the nature of the Astral - you'll notice that in 1e at least, goetics couldn't manifest physically without a Mind 4/Spirit 4 patterning effect to turn them from astral being to spirit. In the Summoner's book, all the goetic summons could never materialize. They can only use their Numina and Influences from Twilight. I'm assuming that's carrying forwards into 2e. The Astral can affect the physical, but it cannot directly manifest physically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:23:48-07:00","id":547268,"title":"","content":"It's not a societal or even a magical law, but a secret world of monsters is still a theme of the larger World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> That aside, being creatures of <i>nightmare</i>, there's something wholly disquieting about the being grabbed by a man-just a man- and you can feel the suckers of a giant tentacle breaking your bones. Even more disturbing, there are those marks after the assaullt-but his hand is <i>always</i> a hand. What the <i>hell </i>is going on here?<br /> <br /> A woman leaps an impossible distance. You don't know how she did it. It's impossible. You used a cable, she has nothing. You heard the beating of mighty wings as she landed, but there's <i>nothing</i> <i>there</i> to make the sound. As she glares with a vicious grin, you have to ask yourself when you'll wake up.<br /> <br /> We're a species reliant on our senses, particularly sight. The most discordant thing you can do, then, the one that blends dreams and reality, is to make the signals contradict each other. You smell the brine in the Desert. You feel the claws on a model's hand. You can taste battery acid on top of the mountain, <i>and there's never anything there</i>.<br /> <br /> So it makes perfect sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-04-2015, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T10:42:32-07:00","id":547308,"title":"","content":"They're entirely visible depending on the effect. We've been over this. If you spend satiety for Infestation, then people are going to bloody notice you turned into a swarm of bugs or what have you. If you use Dragonfire people are going to notice you are <i>breathing fire</i>. If you spend satiety with Limb From Limb, everyone can glimpse the soul looming over you. With Low Satiety, Unbreakable visibly makes your skin seem more leathery, or scaley or whatever.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter that ordinary people can't see the Soul when these powers are called on with Satiety use. They risk the masquerade as much as anything else that destructive or obvious. The reason why Atavisms usally have no obvious, physical changes to the Beast's mostly human body is because they're not <i>physical characteristics it acquires</i>. They're the aspects of the Begotten's Soul <i>seeping into the physical world </i><i>through their flesh.</i><br /> <br /> Anyone with supernatural sensitivity can perceive the Soul when satiety is used to power an atavism, because the Beast is drawing so much of its power to them. It does not, however, take that to notice what it causes.<br /> <br /> I don't get why you think this is counterintuitive. Also see the explanations above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:15:48-07:00","id":547353,"title":"","content":"Remember, you're a spiritual nightmare confined by a pretty little flesh bubble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:35:38-07:00","id":547369,"title":"","content":"I read it as &quot;Normal&quot; people can't See the Cause.. but they See the Effect.. and that would be more terrifying too see Honestly. Anyone who has ANY form of Extra Sense (Vampires, Werewolves etc) See the full effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T14:26:33-07:00","id":547522,"title":"","content":"The Atavisms do risk the cover of masquerade and also they can be in part sensed by other supernaturals;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beings with supernatural senses, however, catch a glimpse of the Soul when the Beast activates<br /> an Atavism. This includes any supernatural creature (vampire, werewolf, changeling, Sin-Eater,<br /> etc.), normal human beings with the Unseen Sense Merit (no matter what it usually detects),<br /> Heroes, ephemeral beings (see p. XX) and anyone else with sensitivity to otherworldly<br /> phenomena at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.<br /> <br /> Glimpsing the Soul in this way doesn\u2019t grant the witness any real understanding of what he is<br /> seeing. The witness sees the Eshmaki take a deep breath and then exhale a gout of blue fire, but<br /> if he is at all supernaturally aware, he always sees the mighty dragon superimposed over the<br /> Beast\u2019s mortal form, unleashing its hellish breath. The Makara activates Monster From the Deep<br /> and everyone in the room feels the pressure of the tentacles around their necks, but only the<br /> Beast\u2019s Promethean companion actually sees the kraken lurking below. </div> </div> </div>Satiety Expenditure is also stated to cause rather obvious effects compared to the usual use of the Atavisms, as stated above in the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T05:57:28-07:00","id":548414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=547522#post547522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Atavisms do risk the cover of masquerade and also they can be in part sensed by other supernaturals;</div> </div> </div> </div>On normal usage - no. becuase &quot;Masquared risk&quot; is when normal humans can see something as supernatural. In <b>Mage</b> terms, when Sleepers will be confronted with the Lie. On normal conditions, Atavisms are not &quot;Masquared breach&quot; as supernatural effects are not visible. All WoD games assume that other supernaturals ( like werewolves and mages in vampire games ) are taken outside of &quot;Masquerade restrictions&quot; as they are monsters also.<br /> <br /> With Satiety Atavisms become almost &quot;shapeshiftng&quot; powers, I envision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T06:49:54-07:00","id":548451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=548414#post548414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With Satiety Atavisms become almost &quot;shapeshiftng&quot; powers, I envision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them, certainly. Others look more like telekinesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T08:57:14-07:00","id":550209,"title":"","content":"It seems like Wyrdhamster is under the impression that Atavisms are invisible by choice, as opposed to just because that is how they work. The Beasts have no formal rule of secrecy but their powers are, for the most part, inherently pretty low profile. For instance, blasting someone with a Nightmare mainly just looks (from the outside) like they've suddenly flipped out for no reason.<br /> <br /> I've been explaining it like this: a Beast's human component is like a dimensional intrusion point for a much larger entity. You see the 'normal' person, but when the whole of the being exerts it's power other aspects of it are acting on the world. A vanilla mortal sees nothing change because of the simple fact that nothing HAS changed. An Atavism that allows you to attack with your claws doesn't cause you to grow claws because the claws are already there and always have been, you're simply allowing/forcing them to influence the world around your human focal point. It also explains why low Satiety causes a lot of the physical Atavisms to have more pronounced visible effects on your body, because the hunger is focusing more of your own reality down into the person shape, distorting it with the metaphysical equivalent of surface tension.<br /> <br /> I agree with ArcaneArts, in that I love the way this works and I think it fits perfectly with the themes of the game. It makes Beasts that much more frightening to some poor mortal who meets one. A vampire, or a werewolf, you can understand. You might reject what you're seeing, you'll be horrified that there's this clear monster that shouldn't exist coming at you, but at least some dude turning into a giant wolf monster and then ripping a door apart with their claws makes mechanical sense to your eyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Imagine a 10 year old girl with adorable pigtails looking up at you with cold confidence and being completely unable to shake the visceral certainty that she's 60 feet tall. Imagine that same little girl pounding through a 2 foot thick vault door as if were made of rice paper, barely bothering to break her stride as she stalks after you, leaving size 44 footprints cracked into your flooring and making the walls of the hallway groan and crack at the passage of a massive body she doesn't have.<br /> <br /> Imagine trying to shake down the local health inspector, trying to beat him down when he doesn't budge, and seeing the smug sneer on his face as your bat clangs off his scrawny frame with the same effect it would have had on a tank.<br /> <br /> <br /> No fangs, no strange pallor, no fur, nothing. Just normal. Just anything but normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T03:08:57-07:00","id":554091,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea of shifting shape when using some powers, but that example with the little girl and the inspector was pretty cool. I really think the game works as it's written. I'll let ya know when my game starts in a couple weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T14:42:25-07:00","id":554886,"title":"","content":"The &quot;why&quot; I imagine might not be what you are looking for. I think it is scarier when the cause of the damage is unknown. Watching someone get their throat slit makes you turn away in disgust. Watching someone's throat open up as if it is cut by an invisible knife means you will be more likely frozen, unable to look away, and you will need to change your shorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T18:23:24-07:00","id":556337,"title":"","content":"I am totally picturing scenes from Genocyber now when it comes to Beast... Mainly the first good OVA, not the shabby sequels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T04:13:53-07:00","id":651017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=547262#post547262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, one thing is that the whole masquerade system is generally reinforced by magic, not laws. As the WoD games went on and on, you'll notice there's less and less &quot;laws&quot; over the matter, and more supernatural consequences. Vampires have the mind-bluring Kiss and the mirror effects. Werewolves have Lunacy. Mages avoid it because of 'dox. Prommies to disquiet, changelings to attracting the Others, Mummies to do their cult-brainwashing thing, GtSE to not annoy their geister. In Demon, its to avoid Compromise.<br /> <br /> Secrecy is literally part of their nature. So, tied into that, invisible Atavism might be part of it. You can't go walking down Main Street looking like a dragon. Werewolves cover their shapeshifting with Lunacy. Demons with compromises. And so on. Obvious shapeshifting has its own secrecy laws - in this case, its &quot;no one sees it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Another part of it might be the nature of the Astral - you'll notice that in 1e at least, goetics couldn't manifest physically without a Mind 4/Spirit 4 patterning effect to turn them from astral being to spirit. In the Summoner's book, all the goetic summons could never materialize. They can only use their Numina and Influences from Twilight. I'm assuming that's carrying forwards into 2e. The Astral can affect the physical, but it cannot directly manifest physically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yeah, but with Beast, their whole deal is that they feed on terror. You'd think if society found out their nightmares are walking among them disguised as human beings it would turn the city into an all you can eat buffet. Sure you'd screw over the rest of your extended family, but Beasts are the one splat who might actually benefit from open exposure. Oh, except people will actually believe a Hero's ranting in the future.<br /> <br /> <br /> The introduction to the Namtaru states there actually was a time long ago when Beasts didn't wear human forms. So if they look human now, something made them look human. Just not sure what that is yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-04-2015, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T07:50:16-07:00","id":651182,"title":"","content":"Them and you know, zombies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T08:13:40-07:00","id":651210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=651017#post651017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but with Beast, their whole deal is that they feed on terror. You'd think if society found out their nightmares are walking among them disguised as human beings it would turn the city into an all you can eat buffet. Sure you'd screw over the rest of your extended family, but Beasts are the one splat who might actually benefit from open exposure.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Some forms of terror are fresher than others. The more intense the fear, the more the emotions die. Terror, in its truest sense, is not a static state, but a dynamic one. It is the moment when hope turns to despair.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T10:50:39-07:00","id":651497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=651210#post651210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Some forms of terror are fresher than others. The more intense the fear, the more the emotions die. Terror, in its truest sense, is not a static state, but a dynamic one. It is the moment when hope turns to despair.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Where is that quote from?<br /> <br /> Also, this thread made me think of Atavisms and Nightmares in a new way. I used to think of Beasts as people who were Claimed by super goetics focused on a specific type of fear. But now I see that it's not a fusion of two formerly distinct beings, it was only the super goetic all along. The impression that a Beast starts out as a human is just that, an impression. The bones and muscles are just a cloak for not attracting too much attention, and a conduit for the Horror/Soul/Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Did I really understand it, or is my phrasing wrong somehow?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T11:34:45-07:00","id":651523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=651497#post651497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Where is that quote from?<br /> <br /> Also, this thread made me think of Atavisms and Nightmares in a new way. I used to think of Beasts as people who were Claimed by super goetics focused on a specific type of fear. But now I see that it's not a fusion of two formerly distinct beings, it was only the super goetic all along. The impression that a Beast starts out as a human is just that, an impression. The bones and muscles are just a cloak for not attracting too much attention, and a conduit for the Horror/Soul/Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Did I really understand it, or is my phrasing wrong somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't too far off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:51:49-07:00","id":651668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=651210#post651210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Some forms of terror are fresher than others. The more intense the fear, the more the emotions die. Terror, in its truest sense, is not a static state, but a dynamic one. It is the moment when hope turns to despair.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Gilles de Rais as Caster, Fate/Zero.<br /> <br /> Distubingly awesome man, Bluebeard is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Feast, you are learning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T13:42:26-07:00","id":651744,"title":"","content":"Bluebeard definitely knew how to create an exquisite feast of fear. I particularly enjoyed how he was teaching Ryuunosuke to turn his killing into a true work of art, and even that art can be fleeting and is often destroyed by the masses who don't understand it. I think it'd be a wonderful way to portray the Hunger of Prey at higher satiety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T17:03:38-07:00","id":651936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=651497#post651497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Where is that quote from?<br /> <br /> Also, this thread made me think of Atavisms and Nightmares in a new way. I used to think of Beasts as people who were Claimed by super goetics focused on a specific type of fear. But now I see that it's not a fusion of two formerly distinct beings, it was only the super goetic all along. The impression that a Beast starts out as a human is just that, an impression. The bones and muscles are just a cloak for not attracting too much attention, and a conduit for the Horror/Soul/Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Did I really understand it, or is my phrasing wrong somehow?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That does seem to be the case, much like werewolves. You don't become a werewolf, you're born as one and the truth becomes revealed once you reach a certain stage in your life. Beasts have human bodies but the soul of a monster. The key to becoming a Beast is realizing that you are the nightmare, you have always been the nightmare. Once you embrace it as a part of your being, you're finally connected with your soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T23:15:10-07:00","id":652148,"title":"","content":"... Honestly I just thought they made the atavisms invisible to make it easier to play as a LARP...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T00:36:37-07:00","id":652196,"title":"","content":"I do not speak for Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> So, that said, building RPG's in such a way that they work for both the table and for LARP is often a lot more work than people give credit for, and it wouldn't surprise me if Onyx Path, while still supportive of the LARP community, put less worry into in the moment considering that and letting By Night Studios stress over it.<br /> <br /> Of course, my only compelling argument for that is just trying to imagine the difficulty of playing a demon in a LARP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:47:52-07:00","id":653105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=651017#post651017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but with Beast, their whole deal is that they feed on terror. You'd think if society found out their nightmares are walking among them disguised as human beings it would turn the city into an all you can eat buffet. Sure you'd screw over the rest of your extended family, but Beasts are the one splat who might actually benefit from open exposure. Oh, except people will actually believe a Hero's ranting in the future. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>The first fear, the original terror, is the fear of the unknown. If you know what something is, can put a name to it, understand how it works . . . that's the first step in mastering that fear. I'd say that's why the Beasts don't want to be noticed (well, that, and the danger of angry mobs).<br /> <br /> Now, Beasts want their <i>handiwork</i> noticed - its hard to scare people who aren't paying attention. They need an audience. But they're also like (real world) magicians - they don't want people to actually figure out how it was done (or by whom). Would anyone remember Jack the Ripper, if we knew who he actually was? <br /> <br /> Killing a person is common place, easily rationalized and quickly forgotten. Happens every day. A series of flayed corpses hanging from street lamps, strung up by their own intestines, with no known perp? Now <i>that</i> catches the public's imagination.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T11:54:42-07:00","id":700017,"title":"","content":"I'm with the OP on this one. Yes, I do get and enjoy the idea of not knowing what you're up against, but sometimes you want to Smaug out in all your glory, even if it's for a short time. I know you can quasi manifest in your own home but meh, I want to go full giant once in a while and not be bound by conditions to do it all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8508-phaide","name":"Phaide","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T12:57:27-07:00","id":700052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=700017#post700017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with the OP on this one. Yes, I do get and enjoy the idea of not knowing what you're up against, but sometimes you want to Smaug out in all your glory, even if it's for a short time. I know you can quasi manifest in your own home but meh, I want to go full giant once in a while and not be bound by conditions to do it all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can remove the hoops that you have to jump through in your own games, but I don't want to go full CWoD and have goofy dragon transformations in the middle of Times Square.<br /> <br /> Or, in other words, to each their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T13:28:18-07:00","id":700062,"title":"","content":"Right, but when my players ask me if they can do this I'd like something a little more structured and official than a house rule that could be potentially broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8508-phaide","name":"Phaide","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T13:28:34-07:00","id":700063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547222-why-not-obvious-atavisms?p=700017#post700017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm with the OP on this one. Yes, I do get and enjoy the idea of not knowing what you're up against, but sometimes you want to Smaug out in all your glory, even if it's for a short time. I know you can quasi manifest in your own home but meh, I want to go full giant once in a while and not be bound by conditions to do it all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Wyrdhamster actually had a hack for that...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/603548-beast-horror-form-hack\">Here it is.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":